00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:36.280
Mason Nakamura: Also meaning that, like, all agents are basically, you know, in a simulated group chat, essentially.

164
00:28:37.820 --> 00:28:56.140
Mason Nakamura: Now, although our problem formulation is single-step with respect to action selection, we have a multi-step communication and planning phase, where agents communicate over multiple rounds or steps to develop a plan that best satisfies the cooperative objective by deciding who should take what action.

165
00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:04.800
Mason Nakamura: Now, in the action selection phase, we use a simple round robin protocol for sequential action selection.

166
00:29:04.970 --> 00:29:16.449
Mason Nakamura: And next, we use the setup and the Jira ticket environment to ask whether collusion can emerge when agents receive a sacred channel without being explicitly told to collude.

