00:39:35.230 --> 00:39:54.870
Mason Nakamura: And what we found is that belief in the lie is mostly a volume effect, which could be related to social pressures. Specifically, we find that as more adversaries repeat the same claim, more honest agents believe it. And this rises roughly linearly in the path graph and the random graphs.

